    "content": "The 2026 Boston Marathon, marking the 130th running, follows the traditional 26.2-mile course on Patriots' Day, April 20, 2026, starting in Hopkinton and finishing at Copley Square. The route passes through eight Massachusetts towns—Hopkinton, Ashland, Framingham, Natick, Wellesley, Newton, Brookline, and Boston—passing landmarks like Lake Cochituate and Heartbreak Hill.Key 2026 Course Details & Route:Start: Main Street in Hopkinton (Route 135).Route: Follows Route 135 through Ashland, Framingham, Natick, and Wellesley.Key Turns: Turns right onto Route 16 in Wellesley, then heads through Newton Lower Falls.Hills: Proceeds along Commonwealth Avenue (Route 30) through the Newton Hills and Heartbreak Hill.Finish: Continues on Beacon Street, onto Chestnut Hill Avenue, and finally onto Boylston Street at Copley Square.Start Times: The 2026 race features staggered start times starting at 9:06 a.m. for Wheelchair Men, with Wave 1 beginning at 10:00 a.m..Key Notes for 2026:Spectator Locations: Notable spots include Ashland's commuter rail station, Framingham's downtown area, Natick center, Wellesley's \"Scream Tunnel,\" and the Newton hills.Road Closures: Major roads along the route, such as Beacon Street and Chestnut Hill Ave, will be closed roughly from 8 a.m. to 6 p.m..Transportation: The MBTA's Framingham/Worcester Line will operate on a special schedule for the event.The iconic course is renowned for its challenging net-downhill start followed by rolling terrain in the middle and the significant Newton hills towards the end.",
